==Swedish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|sv|svenne banan}}
* {{alt|sv|svennebanan}}

===Etymology===
Used by immigrants in [[w:Sweden|Sweden]] in reference to ethnic Swedes. It originates from a [[nickname]] for ''[[Sven]]''.<sup>[citation needed]</sup>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/ˈsvɛnːɛ/}}

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|c}}

# {{lb|sv|colloquial|sometimes|derogatory|or|jocular}} an ethnic/native [[Swede]] (as opposed to someone with an immigrant background)
#: {{ux|sv|Är han '''svenne'''?|Is he an '''[ethnic/native] Swede'''? [see {{l|sv|vara}} for why there is no particle]}}
#: {{ux|sv|en fest med en massa '''svennar'''|a party with a bunch of '''[ethnic/native] Swedes'''}}

====Usage notes====
Has acquired or developed two different meanings, which sometimes merge. One meaning refers to [[w:ethnicity|ethnicity]], merely indicating that the individual referred to is an [[w:ethnic Swede|ethnic Swede]], and the second meaning indicating that the individual referred to is boring, shy and habitually reserved, in reference to the stereotypical behavior of [[w:ethnic Swedes|ethnic Swedes]]. Because the latter sense is actually a common viewpoint in Sweden, both meanings combined or merged are sometimes used by ethnic Swedes, often ironically.

